<Base title="About | Waking Matter" description="Aditya Vikram Singh’s research and engineering work on agent memory, decisions and evaluation. The background and working approach behind Waking Matter." canonical="https://wakingmatter.com/about/" current="about">
  <main id="content" class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero"><p class="label">About</p><h1>Founded by Aditya Vikram Singh.</h1><p class="lede">Waking Matter is an early research and engineering effort focused on how agents use experience. The work brings together memory infrastructure, decisions under changing conditions and evaluation across repeated tasks.</p></header>
    <div class="prose-page split"><p class="label">Why this work</p><div class="measure">
      <p><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/-aditya-vikram-singh/">Aditya’s</a> earlier work spans strategy at Accenture, venture investing at Rukam Capital and corporate development at Noise. Across those roles, the recurring task was to decide with incomplete information, allocate resources and revise a judgment when the evidence changed.</p>
      <p>At Waking Matter, those questions become systems to build and test. Public work includes <a href="https://github.com/avs-io/agent-memory-contracts">Agent Memory Contracts</a>, which makes the path from source evidence to trusted memory inspectable. The <a href="/research/">research programme</a> asks how that retained state should affect later decisions.</p>
    </div></div>
    <div class="prose-page split"><p class="label">How we work</p><div class="measure">
      <p>We favour explicit state, inspectable decisions and experiments that can overturn an attractive idea. A record of past work earns its place only if it helps with what comes next.</p>
      <p>We are looking for collaborators with recurring workflows where errors, effort and human intervention can be measured. Write to <a href="mailto:hello@wakingmatter.com">hello@wakingmatter.com</a>.</p>
    </div></div>
  </main>
</Base>
